Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Episode: PART 06: THE SUNNY DAY (CHAPTER 05)

====

INT. 200 AMSTERDAM - 65TH FLOOR GRAND BALLROOM - SUNSET

The height of luxury. Crystal chandeliers, black-tie waitstaff, string quartet playing Vivaldi. 

KLAUS STERLING stands in the center of a circle of venture capitalists, holding a crystal glass of Dom Pérignon.

                         KLAUS
          Gentlemen, welcome to the future of vertical urbanism. 
          Self-dampening, self-healing, zero carbon, and fully 
          insulated from whatever chaos happens in the streets below.

A GUEST laughs. Klaus raises his glass.

AT HIS FEET: A hairline crack appears in the white Italian marble floor.

It whispers across the tile like a spiderweb. 

The crystal chandelier overhead CHIMES softly. Then SWAYS two inches to the left.

The string quartet stops playing.

                         GUEST
          Did you feel that?

                         KLAUS
          (smiling smoothly, masking a flash of dread)
          Just the building breathing in the wind. Our tuned mass 
          damper on the 70th floor compensates for everything.

INT. ROOFTOP DAMPER VAULT - FLOOR 70 - CONTINUOUS

The 400-TON STEEL SPHERICAL DAMPER, suspended by massive steel cables, GROANS.

Its hydraulic pistons are locked at maximum extension, venting pressurized oil like a wounded animal.

FADE TO BLACK.
